{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 131, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 removed, node 2 no longer reaches the output, so upgrading edge 1 (which feeds node 2 via the 0->1->2 path) gives almost no gain."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without edge 0, node 1 is disconnected from the input, so edge 2 (1->2) carries nothing and upgrading it is nearly useless."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 0 removed, node 1 receives no signal, so upgrading edge 4 (1->3) has about zero effect."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv with skip loses much more than replacing a 1x1 conv, which skip roughly matches."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv on the direct input-to-output edge where none existed gives a much larger gain than upgrading an existing conv."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing an existing skip on the direct edge with a conv gives a much smaller gain than other replacements."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "A skip on the direct edge 3 already supplies a shortcut, so upgrading edge 5 adds less."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "A skip on the direct edge 3 reduces the marginal benefit of upgrading edge 4 to a 3x3 conv."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing avg_pool gives a clearly smaller gain than replacing none, skip or 1x1 conv on edge 0."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing avg_pool on edge 5 with a 3x3 conv gives a smaller gain, especially on ImageNet16-120, than replacing a 1x1 conv."}], "tok": 31016, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect"], [0